==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|sensitive|ity}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|sensitivities}}

# The quality of being [[sensitive]].
# The [[ability]] of an [[organism]] or [[organ]] to [[respond]] to [[external]] [[stimuli]].
#* {{quote-magazine|year=2013|month=July-August|author=[http://www.americanscientist.org/authors/detail/fenella-saunders Fenella Saunders]|magazine={{w|American Scientist}}
|title=[http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/2013/4/tiny-lenses-see-the-big-picture Tiny Lenses See the Big Picture]
|passage=The single-imaging optic of the mammalian eye offers some distinct visual advantages. Such lenses can take in photons from a wide range of angles, increasing light '''sensitivity'''. They also have high spatial resolution, resolving incoming images in minute detail.}}
# {{lb|en|statistics}} The [[proportion]] of [[individual]]s in a [[population]] that will be correctly identified in a [[binary]] [[classification]] [[test]].
# {{lb|en|electronics}} The [[degree]] of [[response]] of an [[instrument]] to a [[change]] in an [[input]] [[signal]].
# {{lb|en|photography}} The degree of response of a [[film]] etc. to [[light]] of a [[specified]] [[wavelength]].

